Aim
Build a table tennis simulator that declares the winner each time the program runs.

- A match is played between two players.
- A game is won by the first player to reach 11 points, with a lead of at least 2 points.
  (If the score reaches 10-10, play continues until one player leads by 2.)
- For this basic simulator, a match is the best of 3 games. The first player to win 2 games wins the match.
- Point outcomes are simulated randomly. This keeps the program simple; player skill ratings can be added later to make stronger players more likely to win.
- In a real tournament, players compete under the same rules and a match result determines who advances.
- Adjustable player count too?

A tournament is a series of matches used to find an overall winner.
This simulator uses a single-elimination knockout format: players are paired for each round, match winners advance, and players who lose are eliminated.
The last player remaining is the tournament champion. If a round has an odd number of players, one player receives a bye and advances without playing.

Main parts of the program
- Player: stores a player's name and a skill rating.
    (Skill rating will start all on 0 - 5 randomly, then if a player wins a game then they ge another skill point)
- Match: simulates games between two players and records the winner and score.
- Tournament: creates the rounds, pairs players, advances winners, and records the champion.
- Main: creates the players, starts the tournament, and displays the results.

Plan:
1. Create a list of players with names and random skill level (0-5).
2. Shuffle the players so the initial draw is fair and different each run.
3. Pair players in each round and simulate each match point by point.
4. Advance each match winner to the next round; give an unpaired player a bye.
5. Repeat until one player remains.
6. Display each match result and declare the tournament champion.

Testing
- Check that a game ends only when a player has at least 11 points and leads
  by 2.
- Check that a match ends when a player has won 2 games.
- Check that winners advance, losers are eliminated, and byes are handled.
- Check that the tournament finishes with exactly one champion and displays
  that winner on every run.